  "_comment": "FQDN pin test vectors shared by internal/auth/fqdn_test.go and ui/spec/models/api_key_issue_fqdn_spec.rb, so the CLI and the UI accept and normalize the same pins. valid maps input to the stored form: ASCII whitespace trimmed, ASCII-lowercased, one trailing dot dropped. Labels are letters, digits and inner hyphens, 63 characters at most; the whole pin is 253 characters at most after normalizing. A pin is an exact host name or a suffix pin: '*.' and a domain of at least two labels whose last label isn't all digits. '*' is allowed only as that whole first label. An empty input isn't here: the UI requires an FQDN, while the CLI treats an empty --fqdn as an unpinned key.",
